  "deviations_from_ci": [
    "CI runs Ubuntu 24.04; this run is Ubuntu 26.04.1 with CMake 4.2.3, so -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 is required (legacy cmake_minimum_required in 3rd-party/ldacBT/CMakeLists.txt). No repo source changed for this.",
    "Host tools pioasm/elf2uf2 were built with gcc-14/g++-14: /usr/bin/c++ points at clang 22.1.2, which breaks pinned SDK 2.1.1 tools/pioasm/output_format.h (missing <cstdint>) under -Werror-free host C++ compile; CI's gcc did not hit it.",
    "Arm toolchain is the official Arm GNU Toolchain 13.2.rel1 tarball from developer.arm.com, installed under the git-ignored project .tools/ directory. CI uses the Ubuntu noble package gcc-arm-none-eabi 15:13.2.rel1-2 (same major).",
    "ccache, GitHub Actions caches, cache-apt-pkgs installation and sudo-run package scripts were not reproduced. The optional CI 32-bit codec-allocation audit was not run (host lacks 32-bit multilib and sudo).",
    "btfw.py and audit_hcd.py fetched their pinned inputs from raw.githubusercontent.com as CI does; hashes are verified by those tools."
